{
"nodes":[
{"id":"reported-symptoms","type":"group","x":0,"y":256,"width":2128,"height":396,"label":"START HERE / Three reported symptoms · source audit, not recovered session telemetry","color":"2"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout","type":"group","x":0,"y":772,"width":4600,"height":444,"label":"Workout (badminton) recording -> SD -> summary -> (missing) calories/graph","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-passive-calories","type":"group","x":0,"y":1336,"width":3232,"height":444,"label":"Passive / basal calories (missing link)","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps","type":"group","x":0,"y":1900,"width":5512,"height":444,"label":"Step counting -> daily activity -> Activity/Energy UI -> persistence -> phone sync","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate","type":"group","x":0,"y":2464,"width":4144,"height":420,"label":"Heart-rate measurement","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power","type":"group","x":0,"y":3004,"width":4600,"height":420,"label":"Battery sampling -> power policy -> screen-off/sleep","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake","type":"group","x":0,"y":3544,"width":4144,"height":420,"label":"Wake (raise / knock / button / touch) -> display on","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification","type":"group","x":0,"y":4084,"width":4144,"height":396,"label":"Phone notification -> banner -> notifications app -> dismiss sync","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist","type":"group","x":0,"y":4600,"width":3688,"height":420,"label":"Settings change -> prefs -> SD/NVS checkpoint","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-weather","type":"group","x":0,"y":5140,"width":3232,"height":372,"label":"Weather fetch (phone or Wi-Fi)","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-alarm-timer","type":"group","x":0,"y":5632,"width":3232,"height":420,"label":"Alarm / timer firing while the app is closed","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot","type":"group","x":0,"y":6172,"width":4144,"height":396,"label":"Boot sequence","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame","type":"group","x":0,"y":6688,"width":5512,"height":420,"label":"Frame: input -> screen tick -> render -> blur -> flush -> panel","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source","type":"group","x":0,"y":7228,"width":4144,"height":420,"label":"Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover","color":"6"},
{"id":"flow-flow-usb-command","type":"group","x":0,"y":7768,"width":2776,"height":372,"label":"USB host command and SD transfer","color":"6"},
{"id":"atlas-intro","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":3600,"height":160,"text":"**NOS Flows / NOS · 1.43-B**\n\nRead each flow left → right. Arrows show narrative step order, not additional canonical graph edges. Red steps touch a verified gap; a badge lists how many. The three reported symptoms lead the atlas.","color":"5"},
{"id":"complaint-1","type":"text","x":48,"y":356,"width":640,"height":248,"text":"**01 / Badminton recorded no calories**\n\nworkout.energy requires a nonzero body mass. The default is unset; the Start screen does not prompt for it. Actual session settings are not established by this source audit.\n\n[[Calorie trace|Source trace]]\nTrace: `flow-workout`","color":"2"},
{"id":"complaint-2","type":"text","x":744,"y":356,"width":640,"height":248,"text":"**02 / No movement graph for the game**\n\nThe session retains aggregate motion counters, not a time series, and Sports has no session chart. Whole-day step bins do not describe court movement.\n\n[[Calorie trace|Source trace]]\nTrace: `flow-workout`","color":"2"},
{"id":"complaint-3","type":"text","x":1440,"y":356,"width":640,"height":248,"text":"**03 / Passive calories missing from today**\n\nThe daily estimate is steps × 0.04. There is no basal-energy calculation, and workout energy is not merged into that daily total.\n\n[[Calorie trace|Source trace]]\nTrace: `flow-passive-calories`","color":"2"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**01 / Sports**\n\nPick the Badminton profile on SPORT READY (body mass and wrist side come from SETUP), then Start.\n\n[[Sports|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|9 verified gaps]]: G01, G05, G06, G08, G100, G39, G41, G44, G46","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**02 / Workout session engine**\n\nworkout_tick samples HR, steps and motion at 1 Hz, also screen off; checkpoint request every 30 s and on lap or state change.\n\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|13 verified gaps]]: G11, G01, G06, G07, G08, G14, G42, G82, G33, G41, G43, G44, G75","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**03 / Wrist movement episode detector**\n\nboard-sense feeds about 150 Hz IMU; the detector finds wrist-movement bursts and returns valid_ms, movement_ms and burst counts.\n\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**04 / MAX30102 HR driver (ext_hr)**\n\nHR lease renewed each second. Only produces bpm if the unverified MAX30102 strap is fitted.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**05 / workout_sd task**\n\nWrites the 4304 B bank to /sdcard/watch/workouts/workouts.0|1.bin with fsync and readback; a RUNNING session restores as PAUSED.\n\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**06 / SD sports journal (.spt)**\n\nSP_IMU, SP_HEART and SP_ACTIVITY records are queued to sports_sd and written to .spt journals.\n\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|9 verified gaps]]: G11, G06, G107, G111, G35, G43, G51, G60, G87","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**07 / Sports**\n\nFINISH SESSION saves history; SESSION DETAILS shows duration, steps, bursts and energy_kcal_est = MET x 3.5 x kg / 200 x minutes.\n\n[[Sports|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|9 verified gaps]]: G01, G05, G06, G08, G100, G39, G41, G44, G46","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**08 / Background jobs monitor**\n\nJobs shows the sports session row with elapsed, steps and energy_kcal_est.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**09 / Activity service (svc_activity)**\n\nMISSING LINK: workout energy_kcal_est is never merged into the daily kcal (steps x 0.04).\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G04, G05, G07, G16, G18, G30, G117, G119, G31, G32, G33, G34, G52, G53","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-workout-step-09","type":"text","x":4152,"y":872,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**10 / Energy**\n\nMISSING: Energy BURN bins come from SP_ACTIVITY only, so workout calories never reach the Energy chart and there is no workout calorie graph.\n\n[[Energy|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|13 verified gaps]]: G04, G07, G09, G16, G59, G111, G112, G123, G145, G17, G35, G46, G60","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-passive-calories-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":1436,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**01 / nos_prefs (RAM struct)**\n\nProfile fields: sports_mass_kg (set in Sports) and the step goal. Mass is read only by the workout engine, not the daily total.\n\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|15 verified gaps]]: G01, G04, G05, G09, G113, G112, G114, G141, G150, G151, G34, G40, G53, G55, G92","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-passive-calories-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":1436,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**02 / Pedometer and walk detector**\n\nOnly steps and walking reach the activity service; there is no resting or basal source.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-passive-calories-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":1436,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**03 / Activity service (svc_activity)**\n\nMISSING LINK: daily kcal = steps x 0.04 with no BMR or basal term, so a still wrist burns zero.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G04, G05, G07, G16, G18, G30, G117, G119, G31, G32, G33, G34, G52, G53","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-passive-calories-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":1436,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**04 / Sports journal (sensor/event logger)**\n\nSP_ACTIVITY every 60 s records cumulative steps-based kcal.\n\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-passive-calories-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":1436,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**05 / Energy**\n\nBURN bins are increments of that cumulative number, so idle hours are empty; food and water are shown beside them.\n\n[[Energy|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|13 verified gaps]]: G04, G07, G09, G16, G59, G111, G112, G123, G145, G17, G35, G46, G60","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-passive-calories-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":1436,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**06 / Activity**\n\nToday page shows the same steps-based kcal and the 24-column hourly chart.\n\n[[Activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G04, G30, G117, G119, G32, G34","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-passive-calories-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":1436,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**07 / Segment face**\n\nSegment face kcal ring uses the same value.\n\n[[Segment face|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 verified gaps]]: G04, G32, G34, G79, G97","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**01 / QMI8658 IMU (0x6B)**\n\nQMI8658 runs at 500 Hz; board-sense reads an accel/gyro burst about 150 times per second.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|4 verified gaps]]: G10, G42, G104, G133","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**02 / board-sense task**\n\n20 ms loop filters the sample to 3 Hz and hands it to the pedometer; runs with the screen off. It also supplies the local day key via the calendar gate.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G11, G10, G30, G117, G31, G33","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**03 / Pedometer calendar gate**\n\nLocal date from time() + timezone; the count rolls over at local midnight and the gate closes while the timezone changes.\n\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**04 / Pedometer and walk detector**\n\nWalk detector and step counter publish steps, active seconds, walking and valid (valid needs an IMU sample under 250 ms old).\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**05 / Activity service (svc_activity)**\n\nact_tick at 1 Hz (also screen off): km, kcal = steps x 0.04, hourly bins, active minute, 7-day week, midnight rollover.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G04, G05, G07, G16, G18, G30, G117, G119, G31, G32, G33, G34, G52, G53","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**06 / Activity**\n\nActivity copies svc_activity() each tick: steps hero ring, today page (km, kcal, active min, 24 h chart) and week page.\n\n[[Activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G04, G30, G117, G119, G32, G34","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**07 / Energy**\n\nEnergy shows today's kcal and burn bins built from SP_ACTIVITY journal records.\n\n[[Energy|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|13 verified gaps]]: G04, G07, G09, G16, G59, G111, G112, G123, G145, G17, G35, G46, G60","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**08 / board-fs task**\n\nEvery 60 s, only while the display is not ON, saves the 24 B pedometer record; a shutdown flush saves the final count.\n\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|1 verified gaps]]: G57","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**09 / NVS nosact (activity history)**\n\nact_save on the UI task writes nosact (day, week, hourly, active minutes) when dirty after 10 min, and immediately at midnight.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-09","type":"text","x":4152,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**10 / Phone line pump and status reporter**\n\nAfter the phone sends {t:act}, phone_tick pushes {t:act, stp delta, hrm} every N seconds.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G12, G13, G18, G88, G105, G106, G125, G127, G36, G46, G62, G66, G67, G68","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-10","type":"text","x":4608,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**11 / NUS transport and RX line ring**\n\nOutbound GB line is written to the Nordic UART TX characteristic.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-steps-step-11","type":"text","x":5064,"y":2000,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**12 / Phone (Gadgetbridge)**\n\nGadgetbridge records the realtime step and heart-rate stream.\n\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**01 / Strap: MAX30102 HR/SpO2**\n\nMAX30102 strap (optional, unverified on B) produces red/IR FIFO data.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|3 verified gaps]]: G47, G51, G86","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**02 / ext task (strap service)**\n\next task wakes at most every 50 ms and runs hr_service.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**03 / MAX30102 HR driver (ext_hr)**\n\nWith a lease, drains the FIFO every 120 ms and computes bpm, SpO2, quality and on-wrist; the lease expires 8 s after the last hal_hr_get.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**04 / Heart rate**\n\nOpening the app requests a stream lease, shows a 4 s PPG trace and a LOCKED BPM state.\n\n[[Heart rate|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 verified gaps]]: G38, G118, G120, G37, G39","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**05 / Heart aggregation service**\n\nAccepts the locked bpm/spo2 with its acquisition epoch and keeps day min, max and resting.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G18, G38, G118, G36, G37, G40","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**06 / HR history ring (144 samples)**\n\nBackground reads (first at +2 min, then every 10 min, up to 40 s) fill a 144-sample ring. Lost at reboot.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**07 / Heart aggregation service**\n\nheart_tick every 60 s rebuilds the 24 h bins.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G18, G38, G118, G36, G37, G40","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**08 / Home widgets**\n\nHome heart widget and the Split face show bpm_last.\n\n[[Home pager|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-heart-rate-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":2564,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**09 / Phone line pump and status reporter**\n\nThe act stream sends hrm = bpm_last with no age check.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G12, G13, G18, G88, G105, G106, G125, G127, G36, G46, G62, G66, G67, G68","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**01 / Battery ADC (GPIO4, divider 3)**\n\nGPIO4 rail through a divider of 3; there is no charge-status pin.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 verified gaps]]: G12, G13, G122, G123, G48","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**02 / board-sense task**\n\nOnce per second triggers the sampler, with the screen on or off.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G11, G10, G30, G117, G31, G33","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**03 / Battery sampler and percent model**\n\n8 reads, median, EMA 1/5, bat_cal offset, percent model; valid after 10 stable seconds on battery; USB inferred from voltage.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**04 / System status service (svc_sys)**\n\nsys_tick at 1 Hz mirrors percent and charging to screens and sends status to the phone every 10 min or on a 5 percent or charger change.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**05 / Power policy**\n\nLow-battery latch: enter at 15 percent or below, leave at 20 percent or above. Idle target comes from prefs (default sensor_idle=1, so SENSOR).\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**06 / Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF**\n\nAfter sleep_s (default 15 s) with no input, keep-awake screen or finger, the UI loop moves to SENSOR (default), AOD or OFF.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|13 verified gaps]]: G09, G10, G14, G15, G19, G29, G100, G110, G122, G49, G52, G57, G99","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**07 / AMOLED panel 466x466 (CO5300 profile, QSPI)**\n\nBrightness drops to the AOD level, or DISPOFF/SLPIN for OFF.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**08 / DFS / PM locks (80-240 MHz)**\n\nSENSOR and OFF cap the CPU at 80 MHz; services keep ticking once a second.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**09 / Sports journal (sensor/event logger)**\n\nSP_BATTERY every 60 s and SP_RAIL every 1 s are journaled.\n\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-battery-power-step-09","type":"text","x":4152,"y":3104,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**10 / Battery history**\n\nBattery history charts the 24 bins read back from the journal.\n\n[[Energy|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**01 / board-sense task**\n\nIMU samples are filtered and fanned to the wake service and knock detector (screen off included).\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G11, G10, G30, G117, G31, G33","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**02 / Wake service (config, learn, tick)**\n\nRaise-to-wake runs each loop pass (about 50 Hz) when the display is not ON; needs raise_wake, not locked, not low battery.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**03 / Double-knock detector**\n\nA double knock wakes the display (or toggles the lock) when knock_lock is set and the battery is not low.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**04 / BOOT button (GPIO0)**\n\nBOOT press edge through the ISR with 25 ms debounce.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**05 / touch task**\n\nTouch still polled at 25 Hz when off; a finger-down also blocks the screen timeout.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**06 / Power policy**\n\nDecides whether a wake request is allowed (low-battery latch).\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**07 / Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF**\n\nThe UI loop sees any wake source and goes to ON: brightness restored, frames resume, DFS raises to 240 MHz.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|13 verified gaps]]: G09, G10, G14, G15, G19, G29, G100, G110, G122, G49, G52, G57, G99","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**08 / AMOLED panel 466x466 (CO5300 profile, QSPI)**\n\nSLPOUT/DISPON and brightness are sent.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-wake-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":3644,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**09 / Home pager**\n\nHome draws the face with the wake-from-AOD morph.\n\n[[Home pager|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|7 verified gaps]]: G12, G13, G103, G140, G32, G36, G79","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**01 / Phone (Gadgetbridge)**\n\nSends a GB notify line over Nordic UART.\n\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**02 / NUS transport and RX line ring**\n\nAssembles the line (up to 2048 B) and writes it to the 8 KB PSRAM ring.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**03 / Phone line pump and status reporter**\n\nphone_tick drains up to 8 lines per tick; once a second when the screen is off.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G12, G13, G18, G88, G105, G106, G125, G127, G36, G46, G62, G66, G67, G68","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**04 / Gadgetbridge protocol handler (gb.c)**\n\nParses notify, notify~ (update) or notify- (remove).\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**05 / Notifications service**\n\nAdds to the 20-entry RAM store, bumps unread and raises the banner.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|7 verified gaps]]: G19, G20, G26, G27, G125, G65, G66","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**06 / Screen stack and transitions**\n\nBanner overlay with app, title, icon and a tap callback.\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**07 / Notifications**\n\nPull up from the face: cards newest first; tap for detail with OPEN and DISMISS; swipe or CLEAR ALL.\n\n[[Notifications|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 verified gaps]]: G19, G23, G65, G66, G77","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**08 / Notifications service**\n\nDismiss removes the entry; nothing is persisted.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|7 verified gaps]]: G19, G20, G26, G27, G125, G65, G66","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-notification-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":4184,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**09 / Phone line pump and status reporter**\n\nSends {t:notify, id, n:DISMISS|OPEN} back to the phone.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G12, G13, G18, G88, G105, G106, G125, G127, G36, G46, G62, G66, G67, G68","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":4700,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**01 / Settings**\n\nA row edit writes the nos_prefs field directly and calls prefs_save().\n\n[[Settings|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G05, G113, G50, G72, G93, G112, G114, G115, G116, G149, G150, G49, G55, G74","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":4700,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**02 / Preferences service (nos_prefs)**\n\nMarks dirty. prefs_tick flushes 2 s after the last edit, 10 s at most, retry 5 s, and only when the persistence window is open.\n\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":4700,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**03 / Live pref application**\n\nMeanwhile the main loop applies the new value live: brightness, sleep timeout, fps cap, radios, timezone.\n\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":4700,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**04 / hal_store (NVS + SD routing)**\n\nsave_checked('nosprefs') routes to the SD banks first.\n\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|10 verified gaps]]: G16, G25, G52, G53, G54, G55, G56, G57, G71, G90","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":4700,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**05 / SD settings bank writer**\n\nWrites the alternating 276 B checksummed bank with fsync and readback under the mount lease and SD lock.\n\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":4700,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**06 / SD settings banks (settings.0/1.bin)**\n\nsettings.0.bin / settings.1.bin on SD are authoritative on B and loaded into RAM at boot.\n\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":4700,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**07 / NVS nosprefs mirror**\n\nNVS nosprefs is the mirror and card-absent fallback. A failed SD save stays dirty and retries.\n\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-settings-persist-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":4700,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**08 / Restart / Power off**\n\nRestart and power off flush prefs before parking.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-weather-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":5240,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**01 / Phone (Gadgetbridge)**\n\nPhone path: pushes a weather JSON (Kelvin temp, code, forecast) over GB.\n\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-weather-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":5240,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**02 / Gadgetbridge protocol handler (gb.c)**\n\nHands the weather line to the weather service.\n\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-weather-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":5240,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**03 / weather task**\n\nWi-Fi path: 1 s poll; fetches every 1800 s (60 s after failure) when Wi-Fi is up, a location exists and the clock is valid.\n\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-weather-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":5240,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**04 / NVS weather_loc (44 B)**\n\nBROKEN PREREQUISITE: weather_loc must already be in NVS; nothing in the built NOS writes it (hal_weather_set_location has no caller).\n\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"flow-flow-weather-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":5240,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**05 / Open-Meteo fetcher (weather_service.c)**\n\nRequests Open-Meteo for the stored lat/lon and parses the forecast.\n\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-weather-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":5240,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**06 / Weather service (source merge)**\n\nwx_tick every 10 s prefers phone data under 3 h old, else the Wi-Fi snapshot. RAM only.\n\n[[Services hub|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 verified gaps]]: G25, G128, G69, G70, G71","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-weather-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":5240,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**07 / Weather**\n\nWeather app, Home widget and the Split face TMP row display the result.\n\n[[Weather|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 verified gaps]]: G25, G128, G69, G70, G71","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-alarm-timer-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":5732,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**01 / Alarms**\n\nThe alarm was set earlier; svc_alarm_save wrote nosalarm to NVS.\n\n[[Alarms|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|3 verified gaps]]: G126, G62, G63","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-alarm-timer-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":5732,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**02 / main / app_main UI loop**\n\nWith the screen off the loop runs at 50 Hz and calls nos_bg_tick(1.0) once a second.\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|3 verified gaps]]: G21, G130, G53","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-alarm-timer-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":5732,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**03 / Services hub (svc_init / svc_tick)**\n\nsvc_tick runs alarm_tick (local hour:minute and weekday) and the timer end check.\n\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-alarm-timer-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":5732,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**04 / Alarms service**\n\nMatching alarm fires (timer uses a monotonic end time and fires the same way via svc-timer).\n\n[[Services hub|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|11 verified gaps]]: G15, G20, G23, G72, G88, G54, G62, G63, G64, G73, G75","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-alarm-timer-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":5732,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**05 / Ringer and ring-screen manager**\n\nArbiter find > call > alarm > timer: pushes the ring screen and repeats haptic and sound every 2 s.\n\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-alarm-timer-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":5732,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**06 / Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF**\n\nThe ring screen carries SCR_KEEPAWAKE, which forces the display ON.\n\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|13 verified gaps]]: G09, G10, G14, G15, G19, G29, G100, G110, G122, G49, G52, G57, G99","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-alarm-timer-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":5732,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**07 / Alarm ring screen**\n\nSlide to stop or snooze 9 minutes; the timer's TIME'S UP offers STOP and +1 MIN; ring times out after 60 s.\n\n[[Alarms|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**01 / main / app_main UI loop**\n\napp_main starts: pacing timer, flush/touch/cmd tasks, hardware init.\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|3 verified gaps]]: G21, G130, G53","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**02 / Board device layer (board.c)**\n\nInitialises I2C devices, touch, IMU and the SD mount, and creates board-sense and board-fs.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**03 / RTC trust and write-back**\n\nboard_restore_clock trusts the PCF85063 (OS and 12-hour bits rejected) and sets the system clock.\n\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**04 / Preferences service (nos_prefs)**\n\nLoads nosprefs from the SD banks, falling back to NVS (via hal_store); legacy cfg is loaded too.\n\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**05 / dotbake task**\n\nPrebakes dot masks and the orrery shade table on core 1.\n\n[[Followup 4 - Uncovered built files- blur pipeline, orrery shade, fonts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**06 / Services hub (svc_init / svc_tick)**\n\nsvc_init clears the notification store, restores nosact, nosalarm, the pedometer and workout banks, and starts the weather task.\n\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**07 / App registry and boot**\n\nnos_apps_boot pushes the boot screen.\n\n[[Shell and faces|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**08 / Boot screen**\n\n43 frames (about 1.1 s at 40 Hz): 49 dots form NOS; touch or button skips.\n\n[[Boot screen|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|2 verified gaps]]: G72, G140","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-boot-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":6272,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**09 / Home pager**\n\nHands over to Home with the face build-in; the face page is the root.\n\n[[Home pager|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|7 verified gaps]]: G12, G13, G103, G140, G32, G36, G79","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**01 / FT3168 touch (0x38)**\n\nTouch polled every 10 ms when ON; native coordinates map to the rotated UI as (465-y, x).\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|2 verified gaps]]: G10, G83","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**02 / touch task**\n\nPolls FT3168 and pushes points into a ring; the UI loop drains it.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**03 / main / app_main UI loop**\n\ntouch_drain empties the 16-entry ring and picks up button flags.\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|3 verified gaps]]: G21, G130, G53","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**04 / Input recogniser and router**\n\nRecognises taps, drags, back-swipes and button click, double or long press.\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**05 / nos_frame_run / frame_run**\n\nframe_run: nos_bg_tick(dt) for services, then transitions and the tick of the top screen (dt bounded to 100 ms).\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|10 verified gaps]]: G101, G19, G21, G22, G50, G108, G129, G130, G151, G152","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**06 / Scene record, damage diff and stripe raster**\n\nScreens draw into the command record; hashes are diffed so only damaged 16-row stripes are rasterised into DRAM.\n\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 verified gaps]]: G132, G77, G78, G79, G80","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**07 / Layer cache (retained rasters)**\n\nA valid retained layer is blitted instead of redrawn.\n\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**08 / Live motion blur gate and kernels**\n\nLive blur is gated off on device (NOS_RENDER_SHARP=1); only the kblur card cache still bakes.\n\n[[Followup 4 - Uncovered built files- blur pipeline, orrery shade, fonts|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|3 verified gaps]]: G132, G77, G78","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**09 / Display flush and QSPI panel driver**\n\nStripe job and JOB_FENCE are queued to the flush task (depth 3).\n\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-09","type":"text","x":4152,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**10 / flush task**\n\nRotates the stripe CCW into the DMA buffers and draws it over QSPI at 80 MHz.\n\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|2 verified gaps]]: G22, G133","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-10","type":"text","x":4608,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**11 / AMOLED panel 466x466 (CO5300 profile, QSPI)**\n\nDMA-done credit returns. There is no TE wait on B, so tearing is possible.\n\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-frame-step-11","type":"text","x":5064,"y":6788,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**12 / Frame pacer**\n\nWaits on the pace timer: 60 Hz present cap with a 40 Hz authored clock.\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**01 / PCF85063 RTC (0x51)**\n\nAt boot the chip supplies UTC as BCD; the OS and 12-hour bits are rejected.\n\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G10, G15, G115, G57, G73, G83","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**02 / RTC trust and write-back**\n\nboard_restore_clock sets the system clock.\n\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**03 / Wi-Fi station, setup AP, HTTP server, SNTP**\n\nSNTP corrects the clock about hourly while Wi-Fi is connected.\n\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 verified gaps]]: G25, G26, G89, G135, G90, G92","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**04 / Phone time and timezone sync**\n\nPhone setTime and E.setTimeZone overwrite the clock and tz_min.\n\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**05 / Settings**\n\nSET TIME and the timezone picker also change the clock.\n\n[[Settings|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G05, G113, G50, G72, G93, G112, G114, G115, G116, G149, G150, G49, G55, G74","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**06 / System clock and timezone (hal)**\n\nAny change raises board_clock_changed.\n\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|4 verified gaps]]: G115, G31, G73, G74","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-06","type":"text","x":2784,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**07 / board-fs task**\n\nrtc_maintain writes the new time back to the chip; forced at shutdown.\n\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|1 verified gaps]]: G57","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-07","type":"text","x":3240,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**08 / Pedometer calendar gate**\n\nLocal date from time() + tz; a timezone change closes the gate until the new day is settled.\n\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-time-source-step-08","type":"text","x":3696,"y":7328,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**09 / Activity service (svc_activity)**\n\nact_rollover at local midnight archives the day and saves nosact immediately.\n\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|14 verified gaps]]: G04, G05, G07, G16, G18, G30, G117, G119, G31, G32, G33, G34, G52, G53","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-usb-command-step-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":7868,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**01 / Host tools (flash_watch, sdsync, exports)**\n\nflash_watch, sdsync or an export script sends a framed text command.\n\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|1 verified gaps]]: G24","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-usb-command-step-01","type":"text","x":504,"y":7868,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**02 / USB serial CDC, framing and guard**\n\nLF framing (191 B cap, NUL+LF resync) and the req <id> envelope.\n\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|2 verified gaps]]: G131, G58","color":"1"},
{"id":"flow-flow-usb-command-step-02","type":"text","x":960,"y":7868,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**03 / cmd task**\n\nEvery 50 ms: SDXFER verbs are answered inline; other lines are queued.\n\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-usb-command-step-03","type":"text","x":1416,"y":7868,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**04 / USB command dispatcher (cmd_exec)**\n\nThe UI loop executes about 130 verbs: prefs, gb injection, ext debug, batcal, diag, open screen.\n\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-usb-command-step-04","type":"text","x":1872,"y":7868,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**05 / SD transfer service (SDXFER v=2)**\n\nList/get/put SD files under the mount lease; mutation blocked during OTA.\n\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"flow-flow-usb-command-step-05","type":"text","x":2328,"y":7868,"width":400,"height":224,"text":"**06 / Preferences service (nos_prefs)**\n\nA prefs flush checkpoint runs before flashing so settings are preserved.\n\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"}
],
"edges":[
